$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-6,8),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=8$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8-4)^{2} & =4p(-6-2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(-8) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-2(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-2(0-2) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2+4 \\\\ y & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $2$ and  $6.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395858 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395859 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395860 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395861 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395862 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395859 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395857 1080 #uuid "402f8b77-e682-57ca-9212-0a3e5c1ad08a" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395858 1081 "$2$ and $7$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395858 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395858 1084 #uuid "9aad8bda-3338-5a30-9437-cc3702c58311" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395859 1081 "$2$ and $6$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395859 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395859 1084 #uuid "327b2ad5-797c-54cc-89