s radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395865 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395866 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395867 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395868 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395869 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395869 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395864 1080 #uuid "8bd2771d-4f88-578f-9fd3-675729a93312" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395865 1081 "center: $(-2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395865 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395865 1084 #uuid "e2fe06dc-0609-5053-9367-73d7ebf2fcb3" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395866 1081 "center: $(-2,2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395866 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395866 1084 #uuid "3f353887-7ced-5107-882a-0276e72dd462" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395867 1081 "center: $(2,2)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395867 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395867 1084 #uuid "d0c03ddb-5aef-510c-adf3-fa2a8970e245" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395868 1081 "center: $(2,4)$, radius: $\\frac{13}{2}$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395868 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395868 1084 #uuid "ef5518f9-14b3-5d56-ae49-14acc285d236" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395869 1081 "center: $(2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395869 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395869 1084 #uuid "0ddf99ec-bda7-505b-b4fe-67ffc75b34aa" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395871 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1069 "q-15460" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}=55+10y.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1072 #uuid "bf1d8b4a-8091-5076-a3c1-f3d77fa5e29a" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395870 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2} & =55+10y \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =55 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =55+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,5)$ and its radius is $9.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395872 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395873 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395874 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395875 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395876 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395873 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395871 1080 #uuid "de4e6f08-aad0-5add-9bc8-7a4631ad1e27" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395872 1081 "center: $(1,5)$, radius: $3$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395872 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395872 1084 #uuid "74e6273a-f318-5c34-a052-af10236b8229" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395873 1081 "center: $(-1,5)$, radius: $9$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395873 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395873 1084 #uuid "6ef4fb82-ea8e-583d-9771-d8277b4a76da" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395874 1081 "center: $(5,-1)$, radius: $7$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395874 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395874 1084 #uuid "c6be1a14-c6c9-582a-8aa6-d933eeef50a8" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395875 1081 "center: $(-5,1)$, radius: $4$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395875 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395875 1084 #uuid "ecbea558-c9ab-5f89-80f4-8cdcb2e0f681" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395876 1081 "center: $(-1,-5)$, radius: $9$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395876 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395876 1084 #uuid "91bca4ac-a533-50cd-b79b-78e54b58a746" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395878 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1069 "q-15589" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1071 "The water boils in a pan at a temperature of ${100}^{∘}C.$ The pan with water is then placed to a room with a temperature of ${25}^{∘}C,$ and the temperature of water decreases. After $5$ minutes, it cools to ${90}^{∘}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the water to have a temperature of ${30}^{∘}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature reading $T(t)$ of the water in the pan decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the water starts cooling.*" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1072 #uuid "02ce9872-8986-5e67-bea1-b49d589c24ac" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395877 1074 "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={25}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-25).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-25} & =-k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-25} & =-k\\int dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-25| & =-kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-25>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-25 & ={e}^{-kt+C} \\\\ T-25 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T-25 & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T & =25+K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature was ${100}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=100,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100 & =25+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 100 & =25+K \\\\ K & =75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $T(t):$\n\n$$\nT(t)=25+75{e}^{-kt}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, after $5$ minutes, it cools to ${90}^{∘}C.$ So, applying the condition $T(5)=90,$ we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90 & =25+75{e}^{-5k} \\\\ 65 & =75{e}^{-5k} \\\\ \\frac{13}{15} & ={e}^{-5k} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15}) & =-5k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the water has a temperature of ${30}^{∘}C.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({t}_{1}) & =30 \\\\ 25+75{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =30 \\\\ 75{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =5 \\\\ {e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our value for $k,$ we conclude that the temperature of water will be ${30}^{∘}C$ after\n\n$$\n{t}_{1}=\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{15})}{-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{13}{15})}≈95\\,\\text{min},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest minute." 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395879 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395880 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395881 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395882 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395883 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395880 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395878 1080 #uuid "fca47f9c-32af-5d7e-92a5-e9a1ab61bc65" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395879 1081 "87\\,\\text{min}" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395879 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395879 1084 #uuid "893f4780-2c8b-522b-8087-2fc24822ebd4" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395880 1081 "95\\,\\text{min}" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395880 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 1