#edb/ref 17592186395973 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395972 1069 "q-20512" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395972 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395972 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & 2x+3y+4z=6 \\\\  & 3x+3y+4z=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395972 1072 #uuid "3437106d-95df-5058-942b-4f64c5179bc5" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395972 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=1 \\\\  & y=4 \\\\  & z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=4$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(4)+2(-4)=1\\,⟹\\,x=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5,y=4$, and $z=-4.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨5,4,-4⟩.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395974 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395975 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395976 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395977 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395978 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395976 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395973 1080 #uuid "2a758e48-dc27-560b-a0af-fd01b7ea572b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395974 1081 "⟨1,4,-2⟩" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395974 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395974 1084 #uuid "23b6f110-fbc4-5322-8a05-6366ff4c13c0" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395975 1081 "⟨3,2,-2⟩" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395975 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395975 1084 #uuid "e6302263-6554-5d2f-bdfe-094ceb26b042" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395976 1081 "⟨5,4,-4⟩" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395976 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395976 1084 #uuid "337c9891-a990-5356-ae53-39e28e060932" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395977 1081 "⟨13,-4,-4⟩" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395977 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395977 1084 #uuid "12ab6864-c814-589e-8f72-328eeae44af0" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395978 1081 "⟨-11,4,4⟩" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395978 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395978 1084 #uuid "fa67123d-ee59-563d-90e5-5d86c85b1243" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395980 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1069 "q-20849" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1071 "![](images/c9/c9371d5e2bb921b4f5e58423bbce492f2b555122ee42bd861040b57d01070353.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=2(t+1),\\,y=4{t}^{2},\\,-1\\le t<1,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=0.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1072 #uuid "45b1f64f-9248-57a2-a310-050eb4c80ee5" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395979 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{8t}{2}=4t.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =4(0) \\\\  & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395981 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395982 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395983 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395984 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395985 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395984 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395980 1080 #uuid "56d7a736-a513-51fb-b585-d99caa2d0531" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395981 1081 "3" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395981 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395981 1084 #uuid "05fd7882-e12b-5d1e-bda2-674211a5aad1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395982 1081 "2" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395982 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395982 1084 #uuid "61e0f80f-69b1-578c-857a-82bc0682835a" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395983 1081 "1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395983 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395983 1084 #uuid "26a77c96-4bef-5e82-8889-1c4a9ce7d523" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395984 1081 "0" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395984 1084 #uuid "9c9b090b-3cbc-511c-95ab-35fc8c1fc057" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395985 1081 "-1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395985 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395985 1084 #uuid "d1c50146-0d7c-501d-bf37-4d8d838c3cef" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395987 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1069 "q-21496" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1071 "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+\\frac{48}{x}$ defined for $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ have a local minimum?" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1072 #uuid "6bb098c4-0b9d-56fe-8eb4-70ba83a986f8" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395986 1074 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ on $(0,\\infty )$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-\\frac{48}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-48 & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-16) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)(x+2)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=2$ is a stationary point on $(0,\\infty ).$ Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{1}^{2}}=-45<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-\\frac{48}{{3}^{2}}=27-\\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{65}{3}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=2.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395988 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395989 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395990 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395991 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395992 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395989 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395987 1080 #uuid "5e6ea143-756a-5eb6-a6ed-9e3449dbdb6b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395988 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395988 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395988 1084 #uuid "220c4644-028c-5dcb-955d-3b2d5604dc62" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395989 1081 "2" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395989 1084 #uuid "13e59b84-50f4-570b-b93f-907264edf062" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395990 1081 "1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395