nd{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396275 1072 #uuid "d2b8ad61-9b47-5971-9495-e31b2ea4691b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396275 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396277 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396278 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396279 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396280 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1077 "field-1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396278 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396276 1080 #uuid "7e1c7d9a-e955-5ffd-bbe8-c5635e09bdc8" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396277 1081 "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396277 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396277 1084 #uuid "445c6a63-f339-5ff2-afa4-e26785fbf1f8