\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396429 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396430 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396431 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396432 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396433 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396429 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396428 1080 #uuid "abca09ba-0b0a-5885-90fb-fd1d7d5af56c" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396429 1081 "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $8$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396429 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396429 1084 #uuid "dcb6c4d2-fc5f-560f-9373-4f7a33529527" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396430 1081 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396430 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396430 1084 #uuid "6565345d-7cca-5723-8a4a-06b781ec17a7" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396431 1081 "$20$ and $16$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396431 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396431 1084 #uuid "71576bd8-08e5-58e9-999c-df3860cd2885" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396432 1081 "$10$ and $8$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396432 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396432 1084 #uuid "b48bdeab-9afb-508b-a31f-840d2716535b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396433 1081 "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $2$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396433 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396433 1084 #uuid "7fd4bf3f-6eb6-53a8-9729-d9955e874477" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396435 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1069 "q-7639" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1071 "Consider the ellipse whose equation is ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y=-11.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Its center is $(1,-3)$\nII. The length of the major axis  is $2\\sqrt{2}$\nIII. The length of the minor axis is $4$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1072 #uuid "fd2cdae2-5e26-5778-ab7e-65d79d794e32" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396434 1074 "First, we must group the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x+12y & =-11 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-2x)+(2{y}^{2}+12y) & =-11 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-2x]+2[{y}^{2}+6y] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}]+2[(y+3)^{2}-{3}^{2}] & =-11 \\\\ [(x-1)^{2}-1]+2[(y+3)^{2}-9] & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}-1+2(y+3)^{2}-18 & =-11 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =-11+1+18 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+2(y+3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2\\sqrt{2}>2,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2},$ the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3).$\n\nTherefore,  I and III are true, and II is false." 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396436 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396437 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396438 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396439 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396440 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396437 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396435 1080 #uuid "e14f3866-43ea-5b8f-9948-a2dc29883068" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396436 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396436 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396436 1084 #uuid "f7f334c8-c362-5bc3-bb42-acf3a7888901" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396437 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396437 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396437 1084 #uuid "306281a3-80c8-5e0a-9a37-cd54c88c73c6" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396438 1081 "I only" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396438 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396438 1084 #uuid "5b8c75df-6d72-5de6-8aa7-4da99784ebe0" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396439 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396439 1084 #uuid "b3f7d8da-7727-5a58-ab68-96bc81e72057" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396440 1081 "II only" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396440 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396440 1084 #uuid "ec7d741b-53e6-5079-a8a5-dd4f4717842f" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396442 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1069 "q-7643" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1072 #uuid "85a05273-d7c5-5a81-9a38-af7c6efc1cfa" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396441 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{3}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+12 & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =0,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396443 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396444 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396445 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396446 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396447 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396445 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396442 1080 #uuid "384638bd-72a6-5df4-a17b-400ec33ad1b3" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396443 1081 "(\\pm 3,0)" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396443 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396443 1084 #uuid "02fe5fe7-b348-53e0-8947-15f0c37ed27c" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396444 1081 "(\\pm 2,0)" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396444 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396444 1084 #uuid "2b6bcede-bd93-5e91-b587-867ae663acd1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396445 1081 "$(0,0)$ and $(4,0)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396445 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396445 1084 #uuid "6d0fc8b9-a163-539b-9c0f-8eb06fff83e1" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396446 1081 "$(0,0)$ and $(2,0)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396446 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396446 1084 #uuid "00403835-be99-5078-bb45-9f705d557d03" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396447 1081 "$(-1,0)$ and $(2,0)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396447 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396447 1084 #uuid "185228aa-01c2-5fd7-a5ac-217c7d571287" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396449 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1069 "q-7644" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis." 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1072 #uuid "86de3c58-7ec8-5280-8df9-9b9e42af2697" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396448 1074 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ 3+(y+3)^{2} & =12 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y+3 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-3\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-6\\,,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the points $(0,-6)$ and $(0,0).$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396450 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396451 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396452 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396453 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396454 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396453 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396449 1080 #uuid "c2e54ba7-369d-573d-a4bf-97c68ce7831a" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396450 1081 "$(0,3)$ and $(0,6)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396450 1084 #uuid "1bf73c45-3794-517e-8928-e6a008fbf5ef" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396451 1081 "$(0,-6)$ and $(0,3)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396451 1084 #uuid "65c8299f-0cca-5cc7-9f93-89e41aaadb17" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396452 1081 "$(0,0)$ and $(0,6)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396452 1084 #uuid "a0731f5e-f8ac-5439-971f-5fe3dacb20b5" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396453 1081 "$(0,-6)$ and $(0,0)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186396453 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 131941